&lt;p&gt;The &lt;strong&gt;Knowing, Being, and Doing&lt;/strong&gt; workshop is designed to help you discover your leadership style and how to lead with purpose. You&amp;rsquo;ll explore your personal strengths, leadership approach, and the ways your experiences shape how you engage with others in the world. Through guided reflection and interactive activities, you&amp;rsquo;ll begin to define what it means to lead authentically, inclusively and intentionally.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this workshop, you will:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reflect on your personal strengths and leadership style&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Examine how your lived experiences influence the way you lead and collaborate&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Explore strategies for leading with authenticity, intention, and impact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Connect with peers and share insights in a supportive learning environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This session is a part of the &lt;a href="https://universitylife.columbia.edu/CCI"&gt;Community Citizenship Initiative&lt;/a&gt; (CCI) and is designed for first semester students who want to develop leadership skills grounded in self-awareness and inclusivity. Students attending this workshop will receive credit for CCI and will have their requirement considered complete.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Registration needed, CUID required.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
